---
name: capture-need
description: >-
  Trigger when the user describes a raw need in free text: "we need X", "the problem is Y", "users are asking for Z". Converts unstructured text into a structured requirement@1 draft — id, statement, stakeholder, why, done_when — without asking clarifying questions. Fields that cannot be inferred are omitted, not fabricated. out_of_scope is intentionally left empty for weaver/connect-requirement or a human to fill in.
version: 2.0.0
---

# Weaver — Capture Need

<overview>
The entry point for turning a raw idea or pain point into something a spec can be drafted from. Delegates to `intake`. Every `done_when` criterion must be a testable proposition confirmable from outside the implementation — not a design decision in disguise.
</overview>

<dispatch>
| Agent | Model / Effort | Delegate When |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **intake** | sonnet / medium | A free-text need statement needs converting into a requirement@1 draft. |
</dispatch>

<references>
`shared/schemas/requirement@1.json`
</references>

<io>
**Consumes**: free-text need statement
**Produces**: `requirement@1` draft (fields that couldn't be inferred are omitted, noted in `reasoning`). Route to `weaver/clarify-requirement` to close gaps before `scribe/draft-spec`.
</io>
name: Validate

on:
  pull_request:
  push:
    branches: [main]

jobs:
  validate:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: Validate plugin manifests
        run: |
          jq . marketplace.json > /dev/null
          jq . .claude-plugin/marketplace.json > /dev/null
          jq . plugins/*/plugin.json > /dev/null
          jq . shared/schemas/*.json > /dev/null
          jq . harnesses/codex/catalog.json > /dev/null

      - name: Validate Codex marketplace
        run: |
          python3 -m unittest tests/test_build_codex_marketplace.py -v
          python3 tools/build-codex-marketplace.py --check

      - name: Check version consistency
        run: ./scripts/check-versions.sh

      - name: Check skill doc accuracy
        run: ./scripts/check-skills-doc.sh

      - name: Check Mermaid diagrams render
        run: ./scripts/check-mermaid.sh

      - name: Check reference file size
        run: ./scripts/check-reference-size.sh
{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "requirement@1",
  "title": "Requirement",
  "description": "A structured statement of what needs to be built, why, who it serves, and what done means.",
  "type": "object",
  "required": ["id", "statement", "stakeholder", "why", "done_when"],
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
    "id": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Unique identifier (e.g. REQ-001)"
    },
    "statement": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "What needs to be built, in one sentence"
    },
    "stakeholder": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Who this serves — a role or persona, not a name"
    },
    "why": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "The underlying need or pain point being addressed"
    },
    "done_when": {
      "type": "array",
      "minItems": 1,
      "items": { "type": "string" },
      "description": "Testable conditions that define completion. Each item must be verifiable from the outside."
    },
    "out_of_scope": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": { "type": "string" },
      "description": "Explicitly excluded from this requirement to prevent scope creep"
    },
    "priority": {
      "enum": ["critical", "high", "medium", "low"],
      "description": "Relative priority for sequencing"
    },
    "linked_issues": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": { "type": "string" },
      "description": "Issue URLs or IDs this requirement traces to (GitHub, Linear, Jira)"
    },
    "reasoning": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Agent scratchpad — chain-of-thought during capture. Not consumed downstream."
    }
  }
}
{
